====================================================================================================
T3 — ADVANCE WARNING. REPORTED SEPARATELY AND DELIBERATELY NOT MIXED WITH T1.
====================================================================================================
A T1 pass says the signal is lit DURING a crisis. It is not evidence of any
ability to warn BEFORE one. T3 drops every in-crisis day from the sample, so a
model cannot 'predict' a crisis from inside it.

No-signal distribution is re-derived per horizon (60 draws of an AR(1)
background at the stationary variance, delta=0), because the null's width
depends on the horizon. delta=1.0 sd is also run as the power check.
background phi = 0.9973 (real rv_t_yz lag-1 autocorrelation)

