  The cluster bootstrap resamples the 6 ONSETS with replacement, not the
  positive days. With 6 clusters the interval is wide by construction — that is
  the honest width, and the reason a single pooled AUC overstates precision.
  'wmean per-onset' is the positive-day-weighted mean of the per-onset AUCs; it
  equals the pooled AUC exactly when the negative set is shared, which is the
  arithmetic that licenses the bootstrap.

